      (return nil err))

    (return f nil)))










^{:go/end 217} (go/method SetUnlinkOnClose "SetUnlinkOnClose sets whether the underlying socket file should be removed\nfrom the file system when the listener is closed.\n\nThe default behavior is to unlink the socket file only when package net created it.\nThat is, when the listener and the underlying socket file were created by a call to\nListen or ListenUnix, then by default closing the listener will remove the socket file.\nbut if the listener was created by a call to FileListener to use an already existing\nsocket file, then by default closing the listener will not remove the socket file.\n" [^{:tag (* UnixListener)} l ^bool unlink]
  (set! (.-unlink l) unlink))


